<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Prepare a Raspberry Pi on Pi4J</title><link>https://www.pi4j.com/prepare/</link><description>Recent content in Prepare a Raspberry Pi on Pi4J</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://www.pi4j.com/prepare/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Write OS to SD card</title><link>https://www.pi4j.com/prepare/sd-card/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.pi4j.com/prepare/sd-card/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The SD card will hold the operating system. On the Raspberry Pi website, &lt;a href="https://www.raspberrypi.org/software/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;on the download page, you can&#10;find the Imager tool&lt;/a&gt;. Select the version for your computer, download, and install it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/website-download.png" alt="Imager download"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Start the Imager and follow these steps:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Put the SD Card in your computer&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Device&lt;/strong&gt;: Select your type of board, click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OS&lt;/strong&gt;: Select &amp;ldquo;Raspberry Pi OS (64-bit)&amp;rdquo; (or 32-bit for an older board), click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Storage&lt;/strong&gt;: Select the SD card, click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hostname&lt;/strong&gt;: Fill in a name for your board, click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Localisation&lt;/strong&gt;: Select your city, time zone, and keyboard layout, click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User&lt;/strong&gt;: Fill in a username and password, click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wi-Fi&lt;/strong&gt;: Fill in the name of your Wi-Fi network, and the password, click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote access&lt;/strong&gt;: Enable SSH so you can access the board remotely, click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raspberry Pi Connect&lt;/strong&gt;: Enable this if you want to able to access the board via Raspberry Pi Connect, click &amp;ldquo;Next&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Writing&lt;/strong&gt;: Now you get a short overview of your choices, click &amp;ldquo;Write&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Confirm you want to erase all data from the SD card. Double check you have put the right SD card in your computer and you selected that one in the &lt;strong&gt;Storage&lt;/strong&gt; step. Click &amp;ldquo;I understand, erase and write&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Wait until the writing is finished&amp;hellip;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;You can now take the SD Card out of your computer, and put it in the Raspberry Pi&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="gallery caption-position-bottom caption-effect-slide hover-effect-zoom hover-transition" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageGallery"&gt;&#10;&#9; &#10;&#10;&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://www.pi4j.com/css/hugo-easy-gallery.css" /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-device.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-device.png" alt="Selecting the device"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-device.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Selecting the device&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-os.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-os.png" alt="Selecting the operating system"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-os.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Selecting the operating system&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-storage.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-storage.png" alt="Selecting the SD card"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-storage.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Selecting the SD card&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-hostname.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-hostname.png" alt="Specify the hostname"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-hostname.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Specify the hostname&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-localisation.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-localisation.png" alt="Specify the localization settings"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-localisation.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Specify the localization settings&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-user.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-user.png" alt="Specify the user name and password"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-user.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Specify the user name and password&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-wifi.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-wifi.png" alt="Specify the Wi-Fi settings"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-wifi.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Specify the Wi-Fi settings&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-ssh.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-ssh.png" alt="Enable SSH"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-ssh.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Enable SSH&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-connect.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-connect.png" alt="Enable Connect if needed"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-connect.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Enable Connect if needed&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-write-check.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-write-check.png" alt="Double check before writing"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-write-check.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Double check before writing&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-write-confirm.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-write-confirm.png" alt="Confirm to write"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-write-confirm.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Confirm to write&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-writing.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-writing.png" alt="Writing progress"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-writing.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Writing progress&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="box fancy-figure caption-position-center caption-effect-fade" &gt;&#10; &lt;figure itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="img" style="background-image: url('/assets/prepare/setup/imager-done.png');"&gt;&#10; &lt;img itemprop="thumbnail" src="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-done.png" alt="Done"/&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://www.pi4j.com/assets/prepare/setup/imager-done.png" itemprop="contentUrl"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Done&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;script src="https://www.pi4j.com/js/load-photoswipe.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/photoswipe/4.1.1/photoswipe.min.css" integrity="sha256-sCl5PUOGMLfFYctzDW3MtRib0ctyUvI9Qsmq2wXOeBY=" crossorigin="anonymous" /&gt;&#10;&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/photoswipe/4.1.1/default-skin/default-skin.min.css" integrity="sha256-BFeI1V+Vh1Rk37wswuOYn5lsTcaU96hGaI7OUVCLjPc=" crossorigin="anonymous" /&gt;&#10;&lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/photoswipe/4.1.1/photoswipe.min.js" integrity="sha256-UplRCs9v4KXVJvVY+p+RSo5Q4ilAUXh7kpjyIP5odyc=" crossorigin="anonymous"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10;&lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/photoswipe/4.1.1/photoswipe-ui-default.min.js" integrity="sha256-PWHOlUzc96pMc8ThwRIXPn8yH4NOLu42RQ0b9SpnpFk=" crossorigin="anonymous"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="pswp" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="pswp__bg"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="pswp__scroll-wrap"&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;div class="pswp__container"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__item"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__item"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__item"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;div class="pswp__ui pswp__ui--hidden"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__top-bar"&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;div class="pswp__counter"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="pswp__button pswp__button--close" title="Close (Esc)"&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="pswp__button pswp__button--share" title="Share"&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="pswp__button pswp__button--fs" title="Toggle fullscreen"&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="pswp__button pswp__button--zoom" title="Zoom in/out"&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;div class="pswp__preloader"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__preloader__icn"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__preloader__cut"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__preloader__donut"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__share-modal pswp__share-modal--hidden pswp__single-tap"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__share-tooltip"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="pswp__button pswp__button--arrow--left" title="Previous (arrow left)"&gt;&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="pswp__button pswp__button--arrow--right" title="Next (arrow right)"&gt;&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__caption"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="pswp__caption__center"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>The First Boot</title><link>https://www.pi4j.com/prepare/first-boot/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.pi4j.com/prepare/first-boot/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Put the SD Card with the operating system into the Raspberry Pi, connect a keyboard, mouse, and screen, and power it up!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="notices tip" &gt;&lt;p&gt;If you configured the login, password, WiFi, and SSH settings in the &amp;ldquo;Use OS customisation?&amp;rdquo; part of the Imager tool, you can connect to the Raspberry Pi from another PC via SSH with the username and hostname you filled in: &lt;code&gt;ssh USERNAME@HOSTNAME.local&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="update-the-system"&gt;Update the System&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Yes, even when you just created the SD Card with the latest OS provided by the Imager tool, it is possible that there are updates available.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Install Java and Tools</title><link>https://www.pi4j.com/prepare/install-java/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.pi4j.com/prepare/install-java/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Our Raspberry Pi has started for the first time and we are now ready to add some Java to it!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="notices tip" &gt;&lt;p&gt;As described on the previous page &amp;ldquo;The First Boot&amp;rdquo;, a script can be executed that will do all this at once: &lt;code&gt;curl -sL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pi4J/pi4j-os/main/script/prepare-for-java.sh | bash&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="add-missing-dependencies"&gt;Add Missing Dependencies&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s start with some helper tools that will be useful later.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ sudo apt install -y i2c-tools vim git java-common libxi6 libxrender1 libxtst6&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;i2c-tools&lt;/code&gt;: Tool to help you with I2C commands.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;vim&lt;/code&gt;: Text editor like &lt;code&gt;nano&lt;/code&gt;, preferred by some, hated by others ;-)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;git&lt;/code&gt;: Tool to interact with a Git repository, like GitHub.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;java-common libxi6 libxrender1 libxtst6&lt;/code&gt;: Dependencies of the JDK Debian package.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="install-java"&gt;Install Java&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There are many ways you can install Java. The easiest way to make Java available for both normal use and as root user (&lt;code&gt;sudo&lt;/code&gt;), is the following approach which downloads one of the many distributions that are available.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>